('B2', 'reading-b2-1', 'Measuring a shorter week', 'A software company tested a four-day working week without reducing salaries. Output remained stable, while reported stress fell. Managers initially called the trial an unqualified success. However, the trial coincided with a quieter sales period, and several employees admitted answering messages on their day off. The company extended the experiment into its busiest quarter and introduced a rule against routine contact on non-working days.', 'What remained unchanged during the trial?', 1, '["Salaries and output","Stress and working days","Sales demand and contact rules","Overtime and staff numbers"]'::jsonb, 'Salaries and output'),
('B2', 'reading-b2-1', 'Measuring a shorter week', 'A software company tested a four-day working week without reducing salaries. Output remained stable, while reported stress fell. Managers initially called the trial an unqualified success. However, the trial coincided with a quieter sales period, and several employees admitted answering messages on their day off. The company extended the experiment into its busiest quarter and introduced a rule against routine contact on non-working days.', 'Why should the initial results be treated cautiously?', 2, '["All employees refused to participate","Salaries were reduced","Output was never measured","The trial took place during a quieter period"]'::jsonb, 'The trial took place during a quieter period'),
