('B2', 'reading-b2-4', 'A label with limits', 'A clothing brand advertised a jacket as environmentally friendly because its fabric contained recycled plastic. Independent reviewers welcomed the material choice but noted that the claim said nothing about working conditions, durability or transport emissions. The brand later published more detailed information and replaced the broad label with a precise statement about recycled content. Sales did not rise immediately, yet customer complaints about misleading claims declined.', 'What supported the original environmental claim?', 1, '["Zero transport emissions","The use of recycled plastic","Locally sourced cotton","Guaranteed lifetime repairs"]'::jsonb, 'The use of recycled plastic'),
('B2', 'reading-b2-4', 'A label with limits', 'A clothing brand advertised a jacket as environmentally friendly because its fabric contained recycled plastic. Independent reviewers welcomed the material choice but noted that the claim said nothing about working conditions, durability or transport emissions. The brand later published more detailed information and replaced the broad label with a precise statement about recycled content. Sales did not rise immediately, yet customer complaints about misleading claims declined.', 'What was the reviewers'' main objection?', 2, '["One feature did not justify such a broad claim","The jacket contained no fabric","Recycled materials are always harmful","Customers never read labels"]'::jsonb, 'One feature did not justify such a broad claim'),
('B2', 'reading-b2-4', 'A label with limits', 'A clothing brand advertised a jacket as environmentally friendly because its fabric contained recycled plastic. Independent reviewers welcomed the material choice but noted that the claim said nothing about working conditions, durability or transport emissions. The brand later published more detailed information and replaced the broad label with a precise statement about recycled content. Sales did not rise immediately, yet customer complaints about misleading claims declined.', 'How did the brand change its communication?', 3, '["It removed all product information","It promised immediate sales growth","It denied using recycled plastic","It made the claim more specific"]'::jsonb, 'It made the claim more specific'),
('B2', 'reading-b2-4', 'A label with limits', 'A clothing brand advertised a jacket as environmentally friendly because its fabric contained recycled plastic. Independent reviewers welcomed the material choice but noted that the claim said nothing about working conditions, durability or transport emissions. The brand later published more detailed information and replaced the broad label with a precise statement about recycled content. Sales did not rise immediately, yet customer complaints about misleading claims declined.', 'What happened after the change?', 4, '["All emissions disappeared","Reviewers withdrew every concern","Complaints about misleading claims decreased","Sales immediately doubled"]'::jsonb, 'Complaints about misleading claims decreased'),
('B2', 'reading-b2-4', 'A label with limits', 'A clothing brand advertised a jacket as environmentally friendly because its fabric contained recycled plastic. Independent reviewers welcomed the material choice but noted that the claim said nothing about working conditions, durability or transport emissions. The brand later published more detailed information and replaced the broad label with a precise statement about recycled content. Sales did not rise immediately, yet customer complaints about misleading claims declined.', 'Which conclusion is supported?', 5, '["Customer complaints measure total emissions","Greater precision improved clarity without immediate sales growth","Recycled content guarantees ethical production","Broad labels always increase trust"]'::jsonb, 'Greater precision improved clarity without immediate sales growth'),
('C1', 'reading-c1-1', 'Preserving more than objects', 'A museum returned several ceremonial objects to the community from which they had been taken a century earlier. Critics warned that the decision would impoverish its collection. The curator countered that possession was not the sole basis of scholarship: a new partnership would support joint research and exhibitions designed by community members. The agreement did not resolve every dispute about provenance, but it shifted the relationship from unilateral custody towards shared authority.', 'What assumption underlies the critics'' objection?', 1, '["Keeping the objects is central to the collection''s value","Joint research is already impossible","The objects were newly manufactured","Community members oppose all exhibitions"]'::jsonb, 'Keeping the objects is central to the collection''s value'),
('C1', 'reading-c1-1', 'Preserving more than objects', 'A museum returned several ceremonial objects to the community from which they had been taken a century earlier. Critics warned that the decision would impoverish its collection. The curator countered that possession was not the sole basis of scholarship: a new partnership would support joint research and exhibitions designed by community members. The agreement did not resolve every dispute about provenance, but it shifted the relationship from unilateral custody towards shared authority.', 'How does the curator respond?', 2, '["By denying the objects'' significance","By ending all research","By promising to buy identical objects","By separating scholarly work from ownership"]'::jsonb, 'By separating scholarly work from ownership'),
('C1', 'reading-c1-1', 'Preserving more than objects', 'A museum returned several ceremonial objects to the community from which they had been taken a century earlier. Critics warned that the decision would impoverish its collection. The curator countered that possession was not the sole basis of scholarship: a new partnership would support joint research and exhibitions designed by community members. The agreement did not resolve every dispute about provenance, but it shifted the relationship from unilateral custody towards shared authority.', 'What role will community members have?', 3, '["Approving museum ticket prices","Replacing every researcher","Designing exhibitions","Only providing transport"]'::jsonb, 'Designing exhibitions'),
