('C1', 'reading-c1-2', 'The appeal of a single score', 'The city ranked schools using a single annual performance score. Although the measure made comparisons convenient, it obscured differences in student intake and resources. Some schools redirected time from unmeasured activities to tested subjects. Officials subsequently added contextual information, but kept the ranking. The reform therefore made the table more informative without removing the incentives that had narrowed teaching in the first place.', 'What was the score''s principal advantage?', 1, '["It captured every aspect of learning","It equalised school resources","It removed assessment pressure","It simplified comparisons"]'::jsonb, 'It simplified comparisons'),
('C1', 'reading-c1-2', 'The appeal of a single score', 'The city ranked schools using a single annual performance score. Although the measure made comparisons convenient, it obscured differences in student intake and resources. Some schools redirected time from unmeasured activities to tested subjects. Officials subsequently added contextual information, but kept the ranking. The reform therefore made the table more informative without removing the incentives that had narrowed teaching in the first place.', 'What did the single score obscure?', 2, '["The city''s annual calendar","The number of published rankings","Differences in intake and resources","The existence of tested subjects"]'::jsonb, 'Differences in intake and resources'),
('C1', 'reading-c1-2', 'The appeal of a single score', 'The city ranked schools using a single annual performance score. Although the measure made comparisons convenient, it obscured differences in student intake and resources. Some schools redirected time from unmeasured activities to tested subjects. Officials subsequently added contextual information, but kept the ranking. The reform therefore made the table more informative without removing the incentives that had narrowed teaching in the first place.', 'What unintended response occurred?', 3, '["Officials abandoned the ranking","Schools prioritised measured subjects","Schools stopped all testing","Parents stopped comparing schools"]'::jsonb, 'Schools prioritised measured subjects'),
('C1', 'reading-c1-2', 'The appeal of a single score', 'The city ranked schools using a single annual performance score. Although the measure made comparisons convenient, it obscured differences in student intake and resources. Some schools redirected time from unmeasured activities to tested subjects. Officials subsequently added contextual information, but kept the ranking. The reform therefore made the table more informative without removing the incentives that had narrowed teaching in the first place.', 'Why was the reform limited?', 4, '["It retained the incentives created by ranking","It removed all contextual information","It banned tested subjects","It made comparison impossible"]'::jsonb, 'It retained the incentives created by ranking'),
('C1', 'reading-c1-2', 'The appeal of a single score', 'The city ranked schools using a single annual performance score. Although the measure made comparisons convenient, it obscured differences in student intake and resources. Some schools redirected time from unmeasured activities to tested subjects. Officials subsequently added contextual information, but kept the ranking. The reform therefore made the table more informative without removing the incentives that had narrowed teaching in the first place.', 'Which statement best captures the author''s position?', 5, '["All measurement is inherently useless","Rankings guarantee broader teaching","Schools should never disclose results","Better information alone may not change institutional incentives"]'::jsonb, 'Better information alone may not change institutional incentives'),
('C1', 'reading-c1-3', 'Silence in the archive', 'Researchers studying a coastal town found abundant records of merchants'' negotiations but few accounts written by dock workers. An early history had treated this imbalance as evidence that workers played a minor role in local politics. A later study questioned that inference, arguing that literacy, preservation practices and institutional priorities shaped what survived. It used court testimony and family letters to recover perspectives absent from official minutes, while acknowledging that these sources had biases of their own.', 'What inference did the early history make?', 1, '["Workers wrote most official minutes","All residents had equal literacy","Few surviving accounts implied limited political involvement","Merchants never negotiated"]'::jsonb, 'Few surviving accounts implied limited political involvement'),
('C1', 'reading-c1-3', 'Silence in the archive', 'Researchers studying a coastal town found abundant records of merchants'' negotiations but few accounts written by dock workers. An early history had treated this imbalance as evidence that workers played a minor role in local politics. A later study questioned that inference, arguing that literacy, preservation practices and institutional priorities shaped what survived. It used court testimony and family letters to recover perspectives absent from official minutes, while acknowledging that these sources had biases of their own.', 'What does the later study challenge?', 2, '["The coastal location of the town","The equation of archival absence with historical insignificance","The existence of merchants","The need to consult any documents"]'::jsonb, 'The equation of archival absence with historical insignificance'),
('C1', 'reading-c1-3', 'Silence in the archive', 'Researchers studying a coastal town found abundant records of merchants'' negotiations but few accounts written by dock workers. An early history had treated this imbalance as evidence that workers played a minor role in local politics. A later study questioned that inference, arguing that literacy, preservation practices and institutional priorities shaped what survived. It used court testimony and family letters to recover perspectives absent from official minutes, while acknowledging that these sources had biases of their own.', 'Which factor affected what records survived?', 3, '["Institutional preservation priorities","The researchers'' travel budget","Modern school rankings","The town''s current population"]'::jsonb, 'Institutional preservation priorities'),
('C1', 'reading-c1-3', 'Silence in the archive', 'Researchers studying a coastal town found abundant records of merchants'' negotiations but few accounts written by dock workers. An early history had treated this imbalance as evidence that workers played a minor role in local politics. A later study questioned that inference, arguing that literacy, preservation practices and institutional priorities shaped what survived. It used court testimony and family letters to recover perspectives absent from official minutes, while acknowledging that these sources had biases of their own.', 'Why use court testimony and letters?', 4, '["To eliminate every source of bias","To prove negotiations never occurred","To replace evidence with fiction","To access perspectives missing from official records"]'::jsonb, 'To access perspectives missing from official records'),
('C1', 'reading-c1-3', 'Silence in the archive', 'Researchers studying a coastal town found abundant records of merchants'' negotiations but few accounts written by dock workers. An early history had treated this imbalance as evidence that workers played a minor role in local politics. A later study questioned that inference, arguing that literacy, preservation practices and institutional priorities shaped what survived. It used court testimony and family letters to recover perspectives absent from official minutes, while acknowledging that these sources had biases of their own.', 'What does the final qualification acknowledge?', 5, '["Personal letters cannot be useful","The new study has no evidence","Alternative sources also require critical evaluation","Official minutes are always accurate"]'::jsonb, 'Alternative sources also require critical evaluation'),
('C1', 'reading-c1-4', 'A cautious restoration', 'A conservation group restored a wetland by blocking old drainage channels. Within two years, water levels rose and several bird species returned. Funders described the project as proof that ecological damage could be quickly reversed. The lead scientist was more circumspect: visible improvements were encouraging, but soil recovery and the return of less conspicuous species might take decades. She resisted declaring the site fully restored, not to diminish the achievement, but to protect long-term monitoring from premature withdrawal of support.', 'What intervention was carried out?', 1, '["Soil was replaced every year","Old drainage channels were blocked","New roads were built","All birds were relocated"]'::jsonb, 'Old drainage channels were blocked'),
('C1', 'reading-c1-4', 'A cautious restoration', 'A conservation group restored a wetland by blocking old drainage channels. Within two years, water levels rose and several bird species returned. Funders described the project as proof that ecological damage could be quickly reversed. The lead scientist was more circumspect: visible improvements were encouraging, but soil recovery and the return of less conspicuous species might take decades. She resisted declaring the site fully restored, not to diminish the achievement, but to protect long-term monitoring from premature withdrawal of support.', 'How did funders interpret the early results?', 2, '["As evidence of rapid reversibility of damage","As proof that monitoring was impossible","As evidence that birds had disappeared","As a reason to reopen drainage channels"]'::jsonb, 'As evidence of rapid reversibility of damage'),
('C1', 'reading-c1-4', 'A cautious restoration', 'A conservation group restored a wetland by blocking old drainage channels. Within two years, water levels rose and several bird species returned. Funders described the project as proof that ecological damage could be quickly reversed. The lead scientist was more circumspect: visible improvements were encouraging, but soil recovery and the return of less conspicuous species might take decades. She resisted declaring the site fully restored, not to diminish the achievement, but to protect long-term monitoring from premature withdrawal of support.', 'What does "circumspect" suggest about the scientist?', 3, '["She was indifferent to the results","She was certain the project had failed","She was unaware of the funding","She was cautious in her conclusions"]'::jsonb, 'She was cautious in her conclusions'),
('C1', 'reading-c1-4', 'A cautious restoration', 'A conservation group restored a wetland by blocking old drainage channels. Within two years, water levels rose and several bird species returned. Funders described the project as proof that ecological damage could be quickly reversed. The lead scientist was more circumspect: visible improvements were encouraging, but soil recovery and the return of less conspicuous species might take decades. She resisted declaring the site fully restored, not to diminish the achievement, but to protect long-term monitoring from premature withdrawal of support.', 'Why might full recovery take longer?', 4, '["No birds had returned","The channels remained open","Soil and less visible species recover slowly","Water levels had not changed"]'::jsonb, 'Soil and less visible species recover slowly'),
('C1', 'reading-c1-4', 'A cautious restoration', 'A conservation group restored a wetland by blocking old drainage channels. Within two years, water levels rose and several bird species returned. Funders described the project as proof that ecological damage could be quickly reversed. The lead scientist was more circumspect: visible improvements were encouraging, but soil recovery and the return of less conspicuous species might take decades. She resisted declaring the site fully restored, not to diminish the achievement, but to protect long-term monitoring from premature withdrawal of support.', 'Why resist declaring complete restoration?', 5, '["To increase drainage immediately","To preserve support for long-term monitoring","To deny any improvement had occurred","To stop all further research"]'::jsonb, 'To preserve support for long-term monitoring');
